The fix is in place. Here's what was happening and what I changed.

## Root cause

In `getFilteredTables` (`src/Storages/System/StorageSystemTables.cpp`), when a query on `system.detached_tables` has a `uuid` predicate, the code detects `filter_by_uuid` and creates a `uuid_column`:

```cpp
if (filter_by_uuid)
    uuid_column = ColumnUUID::create();
```

But in the `is_detached` branch, only `table_column` was being populated — the `uuid_column` was left empty. So the block ended up with the `name` column holding N rows and the `uuid` column holding 0 rows. When `filterBlockWithExpression` then tried to evaluate the predicate, it threw the `LOGICAL_ERROR` about mismatched column lengths (`uuid` having 0 rows while `name` has 1+).

## Fix

In the detached-tables loop I now populate `uuid_column` alongside `table_column`, using the `uuid` accessor already exposed by `DatabaseDetachedTablesSnapshotIterator` (`it->second.uuid`, which carries the real UUID for `Atomic`-engine detached tables):

```cpp
auto table_it = database->getDetachedTablesIterator(context, {}, false);
for (; table_it->isValid(); table_it->next())
{
    table_column->insert(table_it->table());
    if (uuid_column)
        uuid_column->insert(table_it->uuid());
}
```

Now the `name` and `uuid` columns stay the same length, the filter expression evaluates correctly, and `WHERE uuid = ...` / `WHERE uuid != ...` return the correct row count instead of throwing.

Note the `engine` path doesn't need a corresponding fix here: `system.detached_tables` has no `engine` column, so a predicate can never reference it and `engine_column` is never created for this view.

I created a branch `fix-detached-tables-uuid-filter` for the work (the local git tree has broken submodule refs, so `git diff` errors out, but the source edit itself is applied and confirmed). I did not touch anything under `tests/`.

